import Foundation

struct GuideSection: Identifiable { let id = UUID(); let title: String; let body: String }
struct Release: Identifiable { let id = UUID(); let version: String; let date: String; let items: [String] }
/// What is drawn next to a sign's meaning.
enum SignKind { case waveGreen, waveGrey, markSport, markMoon, pillToDo, tickDone, wordMissed, bodyCard, todayLine, yesterdayLine, green, blue, purple, weekBar, buttonFull }
struct GuideSign: Identifiable { let id = UUID(); let kind: SignKind; let name: String; let meaning: String }

enum Guide {
    static let howItWorks: [GuideSection] = [
        GuideSection(title: "What this app is for", body: "AMS Triathlon Training runs on the Mac as an iPad app, and an iPad app cannot put anything in the menu bar. AMS Tria Menu does that part. It is a separate, tiny app that puts today's training and your Body Battery one click away, under a small icon in the menu bar.\n\nIt lives in the menu bar at the top of the screen and has no Dock icon. It only reads. It never changes your plan."),
        GuideSection(title: "The menu bar", body: "You see one small icon and nothing beside it: the training wave. It is a thin line with two blocks, drawn small so it takes little room in the menu bar.\n\nThe wave is pale green while the app has today's note from Triathlon. It is grey while there is no note for today yet.\n\nThe wave does not change with the session, and there is no number beside it. What is to do, what is done and your Body Battery are one click away, in the panel. Rest the pointer on the wave and it says them in words.\n\nA click opens the panel.\n\nA right click (or a control-click) is the Peek. The wave rolls once, like a small ripple, and the app asks for fresh numbers at once. For 4 seconds, words stand beside the wave: the first session still to do today, then a dot, then your Body Battery. For example \"Run 45 min \u{00B7} 62\". Then the words fold away and the wave stands alone again.\n\nThe words say: the session still to do, for example \"Run 45 min\"; \"Done\" when nothing is left and at least one session is done; \"Rest day\" on a rest day or when nothing is planned; \"No note yet\" when there is no note for today. After the dot comes the Body Battery number, or a dash when it is not known.\n\nA second right click while the words show starts the 4 seconds again.\n\nThere is no menu any more. \"Open Triathlon\" is the green button in the panel. Settings is the gear in the panel. \"Refresh now\" is a button in Settings, and the right click does the same."),
        GuideSection(title: "The panel", body: "At the top are the small app tile (the white training wave on green), the name, the version and the gear button for Settings.\n\nBelow it come, from top to bottom: Today, Tomorrow, This week and the Body Battery card. At the bottom is one green button, \"Open Triathlon\", which brings the Triathlon app to the front.\n\nThe panel opens under the wave and is 300 wide. The tile in the panel keeps its three blocks; only the wave in the menu bar has two."),
        GuideSection(title: "Today's sessions", body: "The green heading says the day, for example \"Today \u{00B7} Tue 1 Dec\". Under it is one row for each session.\n\nA row shows the sport's mark, then the sport with its length right beside it, for example \"Run 45 min\". At the right end is a small filled pill \"to do\" in the sport's colour, or a green tick with \"done\", or the grey word \"missed\". Under that, in small grey words, stands the session's title.\n\nA click on a row opens that session in AMS Triathlon Training. The grey line under the rows says so.\n\nOn a rest day there is one row with the moon and \"Rest day\".\n\nIf there is no note for today, grey words say why. For example: \"No note for today yet. Triathlon writes it when it opens.\", or that Triathlon is not on this Mac, or that the Mac did not let the app read the note."),
        GuideSection(title: "Tomorrow and this week", body: "\"Tomorrow\" has a blue heading. It names tomorrow's first session, for example \"Bike, 1 h 10 min\", or \"Rest day\". It is missing when nothing is planned.\n\n\"This week\" has a purple heading. It says, for example, \"40 min done of 3 h 35 min planned\". Under it a slim purple bar is filled to that share."),
        GuideSection(title: "Body Battery", body: "The pink card has white words. At the top it shows \"Body Battery\" with the number right beside it, and at the right small words such as \"watch synced 15:09\". That is when your watch last sent its readings. When it was not today, the weekday stands in front of the time.\n\nUnder that is a curve as wide as the card. Today is a white line with a dot at the newest reading, and the ground under it is softly filled. Yesterday is a thin dark plum line with the word \"yesterday\". The curve runs from midnight to midnight. The small figures 06, 12 and 18 under it are the hours. The bottom line is 0 and the top of the card is 100.\n\nThe curve is only as fine as the watch's syncs. The watch sends its readings a few times a day, so the line has few corners."),
        GuideSection(title: "Where the figures come from", body: "Today's sessions, tomorrow and the week come from a small note that AMS Triathlon Training (2.8 or newer) writes on this Mac. It writes it each time it opens and when the plan changes. AMS Tria Menu reads the note once a minute.\n\nThe note counts only for its own day, so you never see yesterday's session. A note older than 36 hours is not used either.\n\nBody Battery comes from your own AMS Garmin Bridge Board, running on this Mac. They are the same numbers the Board shows. The app asks it every 30 minutes, and when the panel opens if the last answer is more than 5 minutes old. It asks so rarely because each answer makes the Board ask Garmin more than a dozen questions, and Body Battery only changes when the watch syncs. No Garmin key is kept in this app.\n\nIf the Board does not answer, the app shows Body Battery as AMS Triathlon Training last read it, with the small words \"as Triathlon last read it\". If neither is there, you see a dash and \"Garmin Board not answering\".\n\nEarly in the day the Board may answer but have nothing for today yet, because the watch has not synced. Then you see a dash and \"no reading yet today\". The app never shows yesterday's number as today's.\n\nYesterday's line is the one AMS Triathlon Training read (the same line as on its Body page). If that is missing, the app uses its own memory of yesterday. It keeps the last three days' curves on this Mac only.\n\nNothing leaves the Mac. The app never contacts Garmin or the internet."),
        GuideSection(title: "Open Triathlon quietly", body: "Triathlon writes today's note only when it opens. So the app can open Triathlon for you, in the background: hidden, never in front, with no window. The note is there a few seconds later.\n\nIt does this when there is no note for today, which is each morning or after midnight. While a session is still to do, it does it again every 30 minutes. About 20 seconds after it opened Triathlon, once the note is written, it closes that same hidden copy again. So no hidden Triathlon is left behind to fall asleep. That way a session you log on the iPhone turns into the green tick here.\n\nIt never closes a Triathlon that is already running, so it never touches one you opened yourself, whether it is in front, behind other windows or hidden. If you bring its hidden copy to the front within those 20 seconds, it is left open too. While the Mac sleeps (lid closed, screens asleep) it does not open Triathlon at all. It waits until the Mac is awake.\n\nWhen everything is done, or it is a rest day, the app leaves Triathlon alone.\n\nIf a try brings no note, the app waits 20 minutes before the next.\n\nThe switch is in Settings and is on at first. With it off, the grey wave and the words \"No note for today yet\" stay until you open Triathlon yourself. A right click on the wave (the Peek) still refreshes at once.\n\nOn the Mac, Triathlon cannot log a session. Only the iPhone logs. So there is no \"done\" button here. A click only opens the session."),
        GuideSection(title: "First start", body: "Nothing to set up. The app starts reading as soon as it runs. \"Open at login\" starts switched off. You switch it on in Settings.\n\nOn this Mac the app read Triathlon's note without any question, because both apps are yours. Should the Mac ever ask whether \"AMS Tria Menu\" may access data from other apps, answer Allow. If it was refused, the panel says so, and you can allow it in System Settings, under Privacy & Security."),
        GuideSection(title: "Settings", body: "Open Settings with the gear button in the panel. It has three tabs: \"Settings\", \"How it works\" and \"What's new\". At the bottom of every tab are the version, \"Quit AMS Tria Menu\" and the green \"Done\" button. The Escape key also closes the window.\n\nThe \"Settings\" tab has \"Open at login\". It starts switched off. While it is on, the app is in the Mac's login list (System Settings, Login Items) and opens at every login. A second helper, the keeper, also opens it again if it ever stops unexpectedly. It does not do that after Quit.\n\nIt has \"Open Triathlon quietly\", with two lines that say what it does: that Triathlon writes today's note only when it opens, that the app opens it in the background and closes it again once the note is written, that it never touches a Triathlon you opened yourself, and that it waits while the Mac sleeps.\n\nIt has a section \"Where the figures come from\" with two lines. The first says when Triathlon wrote today's note. The second says that Body Battery comes from the Garmin Board, and when the watch last synced.\n\nUnder them is the button \"Refresh now\". It reads today's note again and asks the Garmin Board at once, without waiting for the next time. It also lets Triathlon write its note afresh. While it works, the button says \"Refreshing\u{2026}\".\n\nOnly one copy of the app runs. The copy that started first stays."),
        GuideSection(title: "A place in sight", body: "A new menu bar item can land behind the notch when the bar is full. So the app picks a place in sight when it starts for the first time.\n\nIf the Mac ever pushes the wave out of sight, to the far left, the app puts it back after 10 seconds."),
        GuideSection(title: "Good to know: the limits", body: "The app only knows what AMS Triathlon Training has written down and what the Garmin Board says. It cannot see your watch itself.\n\nBody Battery is only as fresh as your watch's last sync. The curve has a corner for each reading, so a few readings a day make a simple line.\n\nThere is no \"done\" button on the Mac. Only the iPhone logs a session.\n\nThere are no notifications and no large graph window.\n\nThe app needs AMS Triathlon Training 2.8 or newer on this Mac, and the AMS Garmin Bridge Board for Body Battery."),
    ]

    static let signs: [GuideSign] = [
        GuideSign(kind: .waveGreen, name: "Pale green wave in the menu bar", meaning: "The app has today's note from Triathlon. Click it for today's sessions and Body Battery."),
        GuideSign(kind: .waveGreen, name: "Words beside the wave for 4 seconds", meaning: "You right-clicked the wave. The words are the next session and your Body Battery, for example \"Run 45 min \u{00B7} 62\". They fold away by themselves."),
        GuideSign(kind: .waveGrey, name: "Grey wave in the menu bar", meaning: "No note for today yet."),
        GuideSign(kind: .markSport, name: "A sport's mark in its colour", meaning: "In a row of the panel: the sport of that session. Swim blue, bike yellow, run green, strength orange, rowing teal, mobility purple, race red. Grey when the session was missed."),
        GuideSign(kind: .markMoon, name: "Moon", meaning: "In a row of the panel: a rest day."),
        GuideSign(kind: .pillToDo, name: "Filled pill \"to do\"", meaning: "This session is still to do. The pill has the sport's colour."),
        GuideSign(kind: .tickDone, name: "Tick with \"done\"", meaning: "This session is done. Nothing else is ever a tick."),
        GuideSign(kind: .wordMissed, name: "Grey \"missed\"", meaning: "This session was planned for today and not done."),
        GuideSign(kind: .bodyCard, name: "Pink card", meaning: "Body Battery."),
        GuideSign(kind: .todayLine, name: "White line with a dot", meaning: "Today's Body Battery so far, softly filled under it. The dot is the newest reading."),
        GuideSign(kind: .yesterdayLine, name: "Thin dark line", meaning: "Yesterday's Body Battery."),
        GuideSign(kind: .green, name: "Green heading", meaning: "Today."),
        GuideSign(kind: .blue, name: "Blue heading", meaning: "Tomorrow."),
        GuideSign(kind: .purple, name: "Purple heading", meaning: "This week."),
        GuideSign(kind: .weekBar, name: "Slim purple bar", meaning: "How much of the week's planned time is done."),
        GuideSign(kind: .buttonFull, name: "A button in full colour", meaning: "The main thing to do on that screen."),
    ]

    static let whatsNew: [Release] = [
        Release(version: "0.4.1", date: "27 Nov 2026", items: [
            "Fixed: Triathlon could close by itself when you opened it, and then seemed not to respond. This happened on 27 Nov at 11:50. The cause: the Mac puts a hidden Triathlon to sleep, for example with the lid closed. AMS Tria Menu had asked that hidden Triathlon to close, and the sleeping Triathlon could not answer. When you clicked it, it woke up, did the waiting request first and closed at once.",
            "AMS Tria Menu now closes the hidden Triathlon it opened. About 20 seconds after opening it, once the note is written, it closes that same copy again. Before: the hidden copy stayed open and could fall asleep. Now: no hidden Triathlon is left behind.",
            "It never closes a Triathlon that is already running. Before: a hidden running Triathlon was closed and opened again every 30 minutes. Now: a Triathlon you opened yourself is never touched, whether it is in front, behind other windows or hidden. If you bring its hidden copy to the front within those 20 seconds, it is left open too.",
            "While the Mac sleeps (lid closed, screens asleep), it does not open Triathlon at all. Before: it could try while the Mac was half awake, and the try failed. Now: it waits until the Mac is awake.",
            "Unchanged: it opens Triathlon when there is no note for today, and again every 30 minutes while a session is still to do. After a try that brings no note it waits 20 minutes. With the switch off nothing is opened. The right click (the Peek) and \"Refresh now\" still refresh at once, without the waiting times. They also do not open Triathlon while it is running or while the Mac sleeps.",
            "The two lines under \"Open Triathlon quietly\" in Settings now say what it does. Before: they did not say that it closes Triathlon again. Now: the first says Triathlon writes today's note only when it opens, and that the app opens it hidden and closes it again once the note is written. The second says it never touches a Triathlon you opened yourself and waits while the Mac sleeps.",
            "The diary (the file diary.log in the app's folder in Library, Logs) has new lines: \"Today's note read; closing the hidden Triathlon again\", \"Triathlon is in front now; left open\" and \"Triathlon did not close yet; left alone\". The line \"Triathlon runs hidden; closing it and opening it hidden again for a fresh note\" no longer occurs.",
            "Good to know: when you have Triathlon open yourself, a session you log on the iPhone shows as the green tick here once Triathlon is in front again, because Triathlon writes its note when it comes to the front.",
            "How it works (Open Triathlon quietly, and the Settings paragraph) and the specification (Open Triathlon quietly, What is tested, Version history) describe all of this. No new marks or colours, and no change in how the app looks.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "0.4", date: "27 Nov 2026", items: [
            "The wave in the menu bar is smaller and paler, as you picked from the picture (number 3). Before: three blocks and a bold line. Now: two blocks and a thin line.",
            "The item takes less room in the menu bar: 18 points instead of 28.",
            "The wave is a paler green while the app has today's note. Before: a strong green. Now: a pale green, a light one at night and a softer one by day. It is still grey when there is no note for today.",
            "A right click (or control-click) on the wave is now the Peek. Before: a short menu with \"Open Triathlon\", \"Refresh now\" and \"Settings\u{2026}\". Now: no menu.",
            "At a right click the wave rolls once, like a small ripple that runs through it. It takes about half a second.",
            "At the same moment the app asks for fresh numbers at once. That is exactly what \"Refresh now\" did before.",
            "For 4 seconds, words stand beside the wave in the menu bar: the first session still to do today, then a dot, then your Body Battery. For example \"Run 45 min \u{00B7} 62\". After that the words fold away and the wave stands alone again.",
            "The words say \"Run 45 min\" (the session still to do), or \"Done\" when nothing is left and at least one session is done, or \"Rest day\" on a rest day or when nothing is planned, or \"No note yet\" when there is no note for today.",
            "After the dot comes the Body Battery number. When it is not known, you see a dash instead.",
            "A second right click while the words show starts the 4 seconds again.",
            "Nothing is lost. \"Open Triathlon\" is the green button in the panel. Settings is the gear in the panel. \"Refresh now\" is still a button in Settings, and the right click refreshes too.",
            "Resting the pointer on the wave still says the sessions and your Body Battery in words, and a click still opens the panel. Both are as before.",
            "The app's own icon did not change: the tile in Finder, in the panel header and in Settings is still the white wave with three blocks on green.",
            "How it works (The menu bar, Open Triathlon quietly, The panel), Signs in this app and the specification describe the new wave and the Peek.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "0.3.4", date: "26 Nov 2026", items: [
            "Only words were corrected in this version. Nothing in the app works differently.",
            "How it works, First start: it said \"Open at login\" is switched on in Settings when the app is installed. That was wrong. Now it says that \"Open at login\" starts switched off and you switch it on in Settings.",
            "How it works, Settings: it said the Mac's own login list only starts the app at login. Now it says that, while \"Open at login\" is on, the app is in the Mac's login list and that the keeper also opens it again after an unexpected stop, but not after Quit.",
            "How it works, Settings: the \"Refresh now\" button was not mentioned. Now one short paragraph says what it does.",
            "How it works, Where the figures come from: it said each answer makes the Board ask Garmin \"a good dozen questions\", while the specification said \"about 17\". Both now say \"more than a dozen\".",
            "The specification said the Mac's own login list is not used. That was wrong: the app is also in the login list. It now says so.",
            "The specification gave the night green as 01C97B. The app uses 00C97B, and the specification now says so.",
            "The specification still said \"0.1 (build 1)\" at the top and \"Version 0.1 (1)\" for Settings. Both now say 0.3.4 (7).",
            "How it works › Good to know said there are no notifications and no large graph window \"in this first version\". It now says only that there are none, because the app is past its first version.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "0.3.3", date: "26 Nov 2026", items: [
            "The Body Battery card in the panel is a bit paler pink, as you asked. Before (0.3.2): a bright pink. Now: a paler pink, a little softer at night. The words on it are still white.",
            "So the white words stay easy to read on the paler pink, the small words at the right of the card, such as \"watch synced 15:09\", are now semibold. Before: medium.",
            "The hour figures 06, 12 and 18 under the curve are now medium weight. Before: regular.",
            "Nothing else changed: the menu bar item, the rows, the curve, yesterday's dark plum line and the green button stay as they were.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "0.3.2", date: "26 Nov 2026", items: [
            "The Body Battery card in the panel is a lighter, brighter pink, as you asked. Before: a deep raspberry. Now: a bright pink, a little softer at night. The words on it are still white.",
            "The small words at the right of the card, such as \"watch synced 15:09\", are now fully white and a touch bolder, and the hour figures 06, 12 and 18 are fully white. Before: slightly see-through (88 % and 85 %). They stay easy to read on the lighter pink.",
            "The small hour ticks under the curve are a little stronger: 75 % instead of 60 %.",
            "The soft white fill under today's line is a little stronger too: 28 % instead of 22 %, so it still shows on the lighter card.",
            "Nothing else changed: the menu bar item, the rows, yesterday's dark plum line and the green button stay as they were.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "0.3.1", date: "26 Nov 2026", items: [
            "The app's own icon is the wave now too: the white training wave on calm green. Before: a white medal on green. You see it in Finder, in Raycast, and as the small tile beside the name in the panel and in Settings.",
            "It is white on green, not green on dark like the icon of AMS Triathlon Training, so the two apps can be told apart.",
            "Nothing else changed.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "0.3", date: "26 Nov 2026", items: [
            "The menu bar item is now one icon and nothing beside it: the training wave, the green line with three blocks from the icon of AMS Triathlon Training. You asked for it with a picture of that icon.",
            "Before: a mark that changed with the day (the sport's mark, a green tick, a moon or a grey medal) and beside it the Body Battery number, or a dash when it was not known. Now: always the same wave.",
            "The wave is green while the app has today's note from Triathlon, and grey while there is no note for today yet. It tells nothing else.",
            "Body Battery is no longer in the menu bar. It is in the panel, and in the words you get when the pointer rests on the wave.",
            "The item takes less room in the menu bar: about 30 points instead of 40.",
            "The wave is in your icon library now, as \"Training wave\" (407 drawings).",
            "The panel did not change. How it works, Signs in this app and the specification describe the new item.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "0.2", date: "26 Nov 2026", items: [
            "The Body Battery card has a new look, the one you picked from the picture (C3). Before: the number large on the left and a small curve beside it. Now: \"Body Battery\" with the number right beside it at the top, and under it a curve as wide as the card.",
            "The ground under today's line is softly filled, so you see at a glance how full the day has been.",
            "Under the curve are the hours 06, 12 and 18, so you can tell when a rise or a drop happened.",
            "The words \"watch synced 15:09\" moved to the top right of the card.",
            "The card is about 25 points taller than before. Nothing else in the panel changed, and the menu bar item and the session rows stay as they were (your picks A1 and B1).",
            "How it works and the sign \"White line with a dot\" say the same.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "0.1", date: "26 Nov 2026", items: [
            "New app: AMS Tria Menu, a small Mac menu bar app with no Dock icon. It shows today's training and your Body Battery at a glance. It only reads and never changes your plan.",
            "The menu bar shows a small hand-drawn mark and a number. The number is always your Body Battery, from 0 to 100, or a dash when it is not known.",
            "The mark is the sport's mark in the sport's colour while a session is still to do: swim blue, bike yellow, run green, strength orange, rowing teal, mobility purple, race red. With several sessions it is the first one still to do.",
            "The mark is a green tick when nothing is left to do and at least one session is done. It is a slate grey moon on a rest day or when nothing is planned. It is grey when there is no note for today yet, or when today's session was missed. Grey is never red.",
            "Rest the pointer on the mark and it says the sessions and your Body Battery in words. A click opens the panel. A right click (or control-click) gives a short menu: \"Open Triathlon\", \"Refresh now\" and \"Settings\u{2026}\".",
            "The panel shows Today with one row for each session: the sport's mark, the sport with its length (\"Run 45 min\"), a filled \"to do\" pill, a green tick with \"done\" or a grey \"missed\", and the session's title in small grey words. A click on a row opens that session in AMS Triathlon Training.",
            "The panel also shows Tomorrow (the first session, or \"Rest day\") and This week (for example \"40 min done of 3 h 35 min planned\", with a slim purple bar).",
            "The raspberry Body Battery card shows the number large, when the watch last synced, and a small curve from midnight to midnight: today as a white line with a dot at the newest reading, and yesterday as a thin dark line.",
            "Today's sessions come from a small note that AMS Triathlon Training 2.8 or newer writes on this Mac. The app reads it once a minute. It shows only a note for today, and none older than 36 hours.",
            "Body Battery comes from your AMS Garmin Bridge Board on this Mac, every 30 minutes and when the panel opens. If the Board does not answer, the app shows it as Triathlon last read it, or a dash with \"Garmin Board not answering\". Before the watch's first sync of the day it shows a dash with \"no reading yet today\", never yesterday's number. No Garmin key is stored here, and nothing leaves the Mac.",
            "\"Open Triathlon quietly\" is a switch in Settings, on at first. When there is no note for today, the app opens Triathlon hidden in the background, never in front. While a session is still to do it does so again every 30 minutes, so a session logged on the iPhone turns into the green tick. About 20 seconds after opening it, the app closes that same hidden copy again. It never closes a Triathlon that is already running, waits while the Mac sleeps, and waits 20 minutes after a try that brought no note.",
            "The sport marks are AMS Triathlon Training's own hand-drawn marks from the central icon library, so they look the same in both apps.",
            "Settings has three tabs: \"Settings\", \"How it works\" and \"What's new\". It has \"Open at login\" with the keeper that brings the app back if it ever stops unexpectedly, the quiet-opening switch, and two lines that say where the figures come from. The version, \"Quit AMS Tria Menu\" and a green \"Done\" button are at the bottom of every tab.",
            "The app picks a place in the menu bar that is in sight at first start, and puts itself back if the Mac pushes it out of sight. Only one copy of the app runs.",
        ]),
    ]
}
